{
  "id": 438017711,
  "iid": 22604,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "nettrace_3gpp_32_423: Use XML_PARSE_NOWARNING.",
  "description": "Note that there's another `xmlReadFile` call in function `pnio_load_gsd_files` (`plugins/epan/profinet/packet-dcerpc-pn-io.c`) which I didn't change because I'm less sure about how it is likely to be used.\n\n----\n\nThe XML_PARSE_NOERROR option does not prevent xmlReadFile from sending warning\nmessages to stderr (at least on Debian bookworm with libxml2\n2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u4).  We don't want them going to stderr, especially when\nfuzzing, where they add a bunch of noise to the output and probably a\nperformance impact too.\n\nThe XML_PARSE_NOWARNING option silences the warnings.",
  "state": "opened",
