          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2933842934,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "So in the above example, does wiretap say \"not mine\" for nettrace (with the version warning coming from xmlReadFile), try to match other file formats (also fail), and then results in a \"capture file format TShark doesn't understands\"?\nMy first thought is that I thought libxml2 had a way to pipe their output to an \"application\" function, where we could hook it up to wslog.  And that would be my suggested fix because I think that failure message is worth capturing (as a wslog \"debug\" level)",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-12-04T17:03:29.893Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-12-04T17:03:29.893Z",
