        {
          "id": 2933975126,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> My first thought is that I thought libxml2 had a way to pipe their output to an \"application\" function, where we could hook it up to wslog\n\nYes, but I think only in libxml2 2.13.0 or later or some such. I think I have a comment to that effect in the pnio plugin.\n\nIt doesn't help people who are still stuck on RHEL 8 (and maybe not even later OSes, due to the saga of libxml2 breaking ABI and API without a soname bump for a few releases.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-12-04T18:09:30.199Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-12-04T18:09:51.004Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 438017711,
