      "id": "0f0e025ac4a4af03b6b9d6aacf5ee14e6014f62c",
      "short_id": "0f0e025a",
      "created_at": "2025-12-04T16:35:45.000+10:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "e2d7324f20834b5db30e0eec0eb7137954241a44"
      ],
      "title": "nettrace_3gpp_32_423: Use XML_PARSE_NOWARNING.",
      "message": "nettrace_3gpp_32_423: Use XML_PARSE_NOWARNING.\n\nThe XML_PARSE_NOERROR option does not prevent xmlReadFile from sending warning\nmessages to stderr (at least on Debian bookworm with libxml2\n2.9.14+dfsg-1.3~deb12u4).  We don't want them going to stderr, especially when\nfuzzing, where they add a bunch of noise to the output and probably a\nperformance impact too.\n\nThe XML_PARSE_NOWARNING option silences the warnings.\n",
      "author_name": "Darius Davis",
      "author_email": "darius-wireshark@free-range.com.au",
      "authored_date": "2025-12-04T15:43:19.000+10:00",
      "committer_name": "Darius Davis",
